      "body": "## Motivation\n\nI was reading the HiCache design doc and hit this line, where MLA is expanded as \"Multi-Layer Attention\":\n\n> ... in contrast, for MLA (Multi-Layer Attention) models, all ranks hold the complete and identical KV data for each token ...\n\nMLA is Multi-Head Latent Attention (DeepSeek's latent attention). This repo already spells it that way in `docs/docs/advanced_features/attention_backend.mdx` — \"The support matrix is split into two parts: MHA (standard attention) and MLA (multi-head latent attention)\" — so the HiCache design doc contradicts the attention-backend doc.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOne line in `docs/docs/advanced_features/hicache_design.mdx`: the acronym expansion is corrected from \"Multi-Layer Attention\" to \"Multi-Head Latent Attention\".\n\nNo technical statement is changed. For MLA, all TP ranks hold the complete and identical KV data for each token, which is why only one rank needs to initiate the write-back.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable — documentation-only change, no model output affected.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable — documentation-only change, no performance impact.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatting: `codespell --config .codespellrc` passes on the touched file; no trailing whitespace and the trailing newline is preserved. The other pre-commit hooks target Python/C++/Rust, so they do not apply to this diff.\n- [ ] Add unit tests — n/a, documentation-only.\n- [x] Update documentation.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results — n/a, documentation-only.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40340989824](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40340989824)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40340989216](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40340989216)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
